   "content": "<p>vi. It expressed the importance of a point by saying it again and again.</p><p>vii. It made the point sink into the mind by giving examples of animals, birds and insects of the earth.</p><p>viii. It aroused reflection and thought through hints and allusions.</p><p>ix. Through the disjointed letters it gave the feeling of the meagreness of human intellect.</p><p>x. By teaching supplications it taught the means of obtaining guidance.</p><p>In the age in which the Quran al-Hakim was revealed, at that time in Arab society there was great fame of poetry and of eloquence and rhetoric. The people of Arabia considered themselves so eloquent and articulate that they were accustomed to call others “‘ajami”, i.e. dumb. The Holy Prophet ﷺ had spent forty years in this same society and had never composed poetry, nor had he been a pupil in front of anyone. But as soon as prophethood was announced, such speech came on the blessed tongue of the Prophet ﷺ that hearing it great eloquent men were left astonished. Although the short-sighted did not openly confess, in their private moments they were astonished and troubled at what kind of speech this was, which is neither poetry nor prose, nor had they ever before heard such speech nor could anyone make such speech. As it were, one aspect of the Quran Pak being a miracle is also this, that a literary language like it, eloquence and rhetoric like it, and a style like it are not in any other book.</p><p>ii. Universality</p><p>The Quran Pak is a miracle with regard to its universality and world-wideness too. Quranic teachings are universal. They are not for some particular area, race or age, but for the whole human race. In its teachings a cosmic quality is found which encompasses all ages and places. This is the only book which is for every area, every age and every nation. Since human nature from the beginning of creation till today is one and will remain one till the Day of Judgement, therefore Quranic teachings are natural. The man of every age feels as if it has been revealed for that very age. This is the reason that Islamic teachings carry within themselves cure, light and guidance for those living in every age, every area and every kind of environment. The saying of the Exalted is:</p>",
