   "content": "<p>يٰٓاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَاۗءَتْكُمْ مَّوْعِظَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَشِفَاۗءٌ لِّمَا فِي الصُّدُوْرِ ڏ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ (یونس:57)</p><p>Translation: O people, there has come to you from your Lord advice, and a cure for the diseases of hearts, and guidance and mercy for the believers.</p><p>This is the inimitability of the Quran al-Hakim, that when Allah Most High revealed it little by little over a period of about twenty-three years according to need, at that time human needs and priorities were something else, and the human needs of today’s age have become of a completely different nature; but Quranic teachings even today are providing the means of right guidance and guidance to every person of faith. It is not that with the passing of time, with needs and priorities changing, Quranic teachings have changed or do not provide complete guidance. This is the reason that as long as Muslims kept acting on the guidance of the Quran Pak and recognised its greatness and excellence, they obtained ascendancy in their age; and when they turned away from the universal teachings of the Quran, they became victims of decline. The blessed saying of the Messenger, Huzoor Akram ﷺ, is that:</p><p>اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَرْفَعُ بِهٰذَا الْكِتَابِ اَقْوَامًا وَّيَضَعُ بِهٖ آخَرِيْنَ (صحیح مسلم)</p><p>Indeed Allah Most High, through this (Quran), grants honour and eminence to many nations, and makes many nations meet disgrace because of heedlessness of this (Quran).</p><p>Hazrat Allama Iqbal, pointing towards this same thing, had said:</p><p>“They were honoured in their age, being Muslims; and you became disgraced, having abandoned the Quran.”</p>",
