   "content": "<p>وَبِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ اَوْفُوْا</p><p>Translation: And fulfil the covenant of Allah.</p><p>Allah Most High has declared breaking a covenant forbidden, whether it is with Allah or with some human being.</p><p>Surah al-Hashr, verse number 7</p><p>مَآ اَفَاۗءَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰي رَسُوْلِهٖ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْقُرٰى فَلِلّٰهِ وَلِلرَّسُوْلِ وَلِذِي الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِ ۙ كَيْ لَا يَكُوْنَ دُوْلَةًۢ بَيْنَ الْاَغْنِيَاۗءِ مِنْكُمْ ۭ وَمَآ اٰتٰىكُمُ الرَّسُوْلُ فَخُذُوْهُ ۤ وَمَا نَهٰىكُمْ عَنْهُ فَانْتَهُوْا ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ۭ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ</p><p>Translation: And whatever property Allah has given His Prophet ﷺ from the people of the towns, it is for Allah and for the Prophet, and for the relatives of the Prophet, and for orphans, and for the needy, and for travellers, so that wealth does not keep circulating only among the rich among you. And whatever the Prophet ﷺ gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it. And keep fearing Allah; indeed Allah is severe in punishment.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed verse there is mention of the distribution of the spoils of war, and along with it the wisdom of this distribution too has been mentioned, so that no disorder comes into anyone’s heart and mind. In the age of ignorance, after war, the greater part of the property that came to hand was taken by the chiefs of the nation, and in the share of ordinary people very little came. In Islam the authority of distributing the spoils was given to the Noble Prophet ﷺ. The following people will be included in the spoils: (1) Allah and His Messenger, (2) the relatives of the Noble Prophet ﷺ, (3) orphans, (4) the needy, (5) travellers. The wisdom of distributing the spoils in this way has been told, that in this way the property will not remain concentrated in a few hands, but rather its circulation will become wider; further, the needs of life of the deprived classes of society, e.g. orphans, the needy and travellers, too … (continued on p.26)</p>",
