   "content": "<p>Explanation</p><p>In this noble verse there is mention of the standing at night of the Noble Prophet ﷺ and his noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them). Allah Most High says that He has knowledge of your and your companions’ standing in the night. It was said: recite the Quran Pak as much as you can with ease, and do not put yourselves into hardship, because sometimes people are also sick and are also on journey, and sometimes in search of livelihood they have also gone to other areas. And some mujahideen will fight in the way of Allah with the enemies of Allah and the rebels (unbelievers). Therefore read as much as you can with ease.</p><p>It was also said: keep establishing prayer, keep paying zakat regularly, and keep spending in the way of Allah with large-heartedness. In this verse spending in the way of Allah has been declared synonymous with giving a loan to Allah. On the Day of Judgement Allah Most High will return this loan greatly increased. Whatever property is spent in the way of Allah, its best reward will be found with Allah Most High. Besides this there is also the command to seek forgiveness. Indeed Allah Most High is most kind and forgiving.</p><p>Surah al-Mutaffifin, verse number 1</p><p>وَيْلٌ لِّلْمُطَفِّفِيْنَ</p><p>Translation: Woe to those who give less in measure and weight.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this noble verse a warning has been sounded for those who make shortage in measure and weight. For such people the word “wayl” has been used, i.e. for them there is ruin; it is a matter of regret and loss.</p><p>In daily dealings those people who, after receiving the full price of their things, make shortage in measure and weight … (continued on p.28)</p>",
