     "text": "In this noble verse there is an indication towards the event of Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him), that the Quran al-Hakim has declared the story of Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) the best story. Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) was the son of Hazrat Ya‘qub (peace be upon him). Hazrat Ya‘qub (peace be upon him) loved him very much, because of which his brothers began to envy him, and taking Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) out of the house, threw him into a well, and coming home told that a wolf had eaten him. Hazrat Ya‘qub (peace be upon him) became extremely grieved. It happened by Allah’s decree that Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) got the kingship of Egypt. During this time Zulaikha too levelled an accusation against Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him), but the accusation levelled against him was proved false.",
