   "content": "<p>(continued from p.30) … invitation accept, they become deserving of those rewards. The purpose of stating the stories of other prophets in the Quran al-Hakim is also this, that the followers of the Noble Prophet ﷺ too learn about the attitudes of previous nations and take a lesson from their end.</p><p>Surah Yusuf, verse number 3</p><p>نَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ اَحْسَنَ الْقَصَصِ بِمَآ اَوْحَيْنَآ اِلَيْكَ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ ڰ وَاِنْ كُنْتَ مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ لَمِنَ الْغٰفِلِيْنَ</p><p>Translation: O Prophet, through this Quran which We have sent to you, We relate to you a very good story; and before this you were unaware.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this noble verse there is an indication towards the event of Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him), that the Quran al-Hakim has declared the story of Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) the best story. Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) was the son of Hazrat Ya‘qub (peace be upon him). Hazrat Ya‘qub (peace be upon him) loved him very much, because of which his brothers began to envy him, and taking Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) out of the house, threw him into a well, and coming home told that a wolf had eaten him. Hazrat Ya‘qub (peace be upon him) became extremely grieved. It happened by Allah’s decree that Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) got the kingship of Egypt. During this time Zulaikha too levelled an accusation against Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him), but the accusation levelled against him was proved false.</p><p>In the event of Hazrat Yusuf (peace be upon him) there are many lessons for us, of which the following are more important:</p><p>a. One should avoid envying others.</p>",
