   "content": "<p>Household management</p><p>Surah al-Baqarah, verse number 83</p><p>وَاِذْ اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَ بَنِيْٓ اِسْرَاۗءِيْلَ لَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ اِلَّا اللّٰهَ ۣ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا وَّذِي الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَقُوْلُوْا لِلنَّاسِ حُسْـنًا وَّاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ ۭ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّنْكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ</p><p>Translation: And when We took a covenant from the Children of Israel that you will not worship anyone except Allah, and you will keep doing good to parents and relatives and orphans and the needy, and will speak good words to people, and keep praying and paying zakat; then, except a few men, all of you turned your faces from this covenant and turned back.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed verse the Children of Israel have been reminded that when Allah took a covenant from them that they would worship Allah alone purely, do good to parents, relatives, orphans and the needy, behave with good conduct with ordinary people and speak good words to them, establish prayer and keep paying zakat, then except a few people no one honoured his covenant and they turned back from their covenant.</p><p>From this noble verse it is proved that to obtain the destination of the goal it is necessary that no one be made a partner with Allah. Worship Him alone. Good conduct should be done with parents. No shortcoming should be left in their service … (continued on p.38)</p>",
