   "content": "<p>وَمَآ اٰتَيْتُمْ مِّنْ رِّبًا لِّيَرْبُوَا۟ فِيْٓ اَمْوَالِ النَّاسِ فَلَا يَرْبُوْا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَمَآ اٰتَيْتُمْ مِّنْ زَكٰوةٍ تُرِيْدُوْنَ وَجْهَ اللّٰهِ فَاُولٰۗىِٕكَ هُمُ الْمُضْعِفُوْنَ (الروم: 39)</p><p>Translation: And the interest that you give so that it may increase in the property of people, it does not increase at all with Allah; and the zakat that you give seeking the pleasure of Allah, that is a cause of blessing, and such people multiply their property many times.</p><p>From the above-mentioned verses it becomes clear that Islam has given very great importance to zakat. For the payment of zakat it is necessary to possess the nisab. On fifty-two and a half tolas of silver, seven and a half tolas of gold, trade goods and accumulated money, if a full year passes, then taking out its fortieth part and giving it in the way of God is called zakat. Besides gold and wealth, zakat has been made obligatory on cattle too.</p><p>Where Islam has fixed the nisab for the payment of zakat, there the heads of expenditure of zakat too have been told. The saying of the Exalted is:</p><p>اِنَّمَا الصَّدَقٰتُ لِلْفُقَرَاۗءِ وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَالْعٰمِلِيْنَ عَلَيْهَا وَالْمُؤَلَّفَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَفِي الرِّقَابِ وَالْغٰرِمِيْنَ وَفِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِ ۭ فَرِيْضَةً مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ۭ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ (التوبہ: 60)</p><p>Translation: Charities, i.e. zakat and alms, are the right of the poor and the destitute and of the workers on charities, and of those people whose hearts are to be won; and in freeing slaves, and in paying the debt of debtors, and in the way of Allah, and in helping travellers too this property should be spent. These heads of expenditure have been fixed by Allah, and Allah is knowing and wise.</p>",
