   "content": "<p>6. Property and wealth surplus to need should be spent in the way of God.</p><p>وَيَسْــَٔلُوْنَكَ مَاذَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ ڛ قُلِ الْعَفْوَ ۭ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ (البقرة: 219)</p><p>Translation: And they ask you which property they should spend in the way of Allah. Say: whatever is more than need. In this way Allah states His injunctions clearly for you so that you think.</p><p>7. From the people to whom zakat and charities are given, it should not be expected that they will always remain grateful or will come to their help in some difficult time. In this connection the following noble verse provides basic guidance.</p><p>يٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تُبْطِلُوْا صَدَقٰتِكُمْ بِالْمَنِّ وَالْاَذٰى (البقرة: 264)</p><p>Translation: Believers! Do not ruin your charities and alms by showing favour and giving hurt.</p><p>8. Wealth and the resources of producing wealth should not be concentrated in a particular class.</p><p>9. Individual ownership will remain subject to collective ownership.</p><p>10. The foundation of the economic system has been kept on public interest.</p><p>The economic system formed by keeping the above-mentioned principles and rules in front provides a guarantee of economic equality in society. If these principles and rules are compared with the principles of socialism and capitalism, then the beauty of the Islamic economic system comes out in front clearly. By acting on these principles, racial, linguistic, geographical and class distinctions get erased. Further, by acting on these golden principles, wealth does not remain limited to particular classes, but rather the general class of society too keeps benefiting from it.</p><p>Social importance</p><p>The motives behind the curtain of any economic system are its real spirit. If the philosophy of that system is based on a corrupt mind … (continued on p.49)</p>",
