   "content": "<p>(continued from p.48) … then its results too come out corrupt, and if the spirit of that economic system is based on human welfare, then as a result the public becomes prosperous.</p><p>The intent of spending in the way of Allah is this, that the classes which are left behind in the economic race on the basis of some reasons, they should be helped and put on their feet. Islam, departing from ancient and modern theories, has given such economic theories as are exactly according to human nature. Since the Islamic principles of economy have been given by the Creator of the earth and the heavens for the good of human beings, therefore these are much better than the economic theories made by man. This is the reason that even after centuries economic unevenness can be removed only by Islamic teachings — not by socialism or capitalism.</p><p>From the social point of view the following benefits and fruits are obtained from spending in the way of Allah:</p><p>1. The concentration of wealth ends, from which speed comes in the circulation of wealth, and in this way the common man too begins to benefit from it.</p><p>2. Through the system of zakat, alms and charities, an atmosphere of mutual love and closeness arises between rich and poor, which is the guarantor of social peace and tranquillity and construction and progress.</p><p>3. Through Islamic economic teachings no individual or group becomes a victim of economic deprivation, from which incidents of theft, robbery and deceit in society are prevented.</p><p>4. The help that deprived classes get from wealthy households and groups makes them shareholders in economic activities, from which economic activities increase and the standard of living of people becomes high.</p><p>5. People benefiting from spending in the way of Allah do not feel malice and envy towards well-to-do individuals; rather, in their heart and mind the spirit of practical struggle gets promotion, and they become ready to take full benefit of their abilities. This positive tendency gives birth to social harmony.</p><p>6. By spending in the way of Allah out of the sustenance given by Allah Most High, attention does not go towards luxury and pleasure; rather, in the service of the creation of God so much comfort and peace is obtained that in the hearts of the rich the love of the needy, orphans, widows, the helpless, the destitute and the unclaimed arises, which ultimately results in social welfare and wellbeing.</p>",
