   "content": "<p>1. Practical enforcement of Islamic laws</p><p>The basic duty of the Islamic state is that it practically enforce Islamic laws, make certain the protection of Islamic symbols, and take solid measures for preventing evils. The saying of the Exalted is:</p><p>اَلَّذِيْنَ اِنْ مَّكَّنّٰهُمْ فِي الْاَرْضِ اَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَمَرُوْا بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَنَهَوْا عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ ۭ وَلِلّٰهِ عَاقِبَةُ الْاُمُوْرِ (الحج: 41)</p><p>Translation: These are the people who, if We give them government in the land, will establish prayer and pay zakat, and command to do good works and forbid evil works; and the end of all works is in the control of Allah alone.</p><p>2. Establishment of the system of justice</p><p>An important duty of the Islamic state is the establishment of a collective system of justice. It should make certain the supremacy of law and its rule, and decide cases according to the pure Shariah. The divine saying is:</p><p>لَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَاَنْزَلْنَا مَعَهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ لِيَقُوْمَ النَّاسُ بِالْقِسْطِ ۚ وَاَنْزَلْنَا الْحَدِيْدَ فِيْهِ بَاْسٌ شَدِيْدٌ وَّمَنَافِعُ لِلنَّاسِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّنْصُرُهٗ وَرُسُلَهٗ بِالْغَيْبِ ۭ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَوِيٌّ عَزِيْزٌ (الحدید: 25)</p><p>Translation: We sent Our messengers with clear signs and revealed upon them books and the balance of justice, so that people may remain established on justice. And We produced iron, in which, with regard to weapons of war, there is very great force too, and for people there are benefits too; and so that Allah may know who, without seeing, helps Allah and His messengers. Indeed Allah is powerful and dominant.</p>",
