   "content": "<p>E. A study of the Sirah of the Messenger ﷺ in the light of the Holy Quran</p><p>Freedom of thought, respect for humanity and the basis of mutual relations</p><p>Man is the best creation of Allah the Exalted. Allah the Exalted has endowed him with unlimited abilities and capabilities. Man has been granted such capabilities that, by using them, he can accomplish astonishing feats. The divine saying is:</p><p>لَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ فِيْٓ اَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيْمٍ (التین: 4)</p><p>Translation: Indeed, We have moulded man in the best form.</p><p>Allah the Exalted sent various prophets and messengers in different eras for the guidance and direction of human beings. In this [chain] of guidance, the Noble Prophet ﷺ was sent last of all. He ﷺ was crowned with the finality of prophethood and sent into the [world], and was made the Prophet for all human beings till the Day of Judgement. After him ﷺ the door of prophethood and messengership was closed forever. The society into which he ﷺ came had fallen into the [utmost] depths of oppression and ignorance. The collective moral decline of the society was such that pride and [arrogance] was displayed over evil and shameless deeds. Such evils had pervaded Arab society that even today mentioning them is a [stain] on the dignity of humanity. The market of disbelief and polytheism was hot. More than three hundred idols had been placed in the Kaaba, and people considered performing the [tawaf] of the Kaaba naked a means of reward. Women and slaves were treated shamefully. The powerful pounced upon the weak just [as] an eagle pounces upon a weak bird.</p><p>The Noble Prophet ﷺ opened his eyes in such a society where freedom of thought, respect for humanity or mutual [love and] harmony had no name or trace far and wide. A few people were certainly there who stayed away from the idolatry of that era. They [were called] hunafa&#x27;. The Noble Prophet ﷺ lived for forty years in this same society and, like an ordinary man, took part in [the] affairs and routines [of life].</p><p>When he ﷺ received the command to announce prophethood, he ﷺ [brought a revolution] in freedom of thought …</p>",
