   "theory": "… such wealth or things which you yourselves would not like when taking them — avoid spending them in the way of Allah too.\n\nThe philosophy of spending in the way of Allah is this very thing: that whatever we earn, we also give some part of it, in the form of zakat, charity and alms, to those servants of Allah who for some reason have become needy, or who for some reason have been left behind us in the economic race.\n\nVerse no. 268\n\nاَلشَّيْطٰنُ يَعِدُكُمُ الْفَقْرَ وَيَاْمُرُكُمْ بِالْفَحْشَآءِ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَعِدُكُمْ مَّغْفِرَةً مِّنْهُ وَفَضْلًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ\n\nTranslation: Satan frightens you with poverty and tells you to do shameless deeds, and Allah promises you His forgiveness and mercy. And Allah is the Possessor of abundance and the Knower of everything.\n\nExplanation\n\nThis noble verse is the continuation of the previous verse. Allah the Exalted says that spending in the way of God is the work of the brave-hearted. Satan casts doubts into the heart of man that by spending in the way of Allah wealth will decrease. Hardship will come and the danger of poverty will increase. Allah says that Satan always incites only to shameless deeds, whereas Allah promises forgiveness and pardon. He is the Knower of all. He understands all creatures well. His mercies are countless; therefore never hold back your hand from spending in the way of God for fear of poverty and hardship. Rather, giving the best part of one's wealth in His way — He is the giver of [abundance and] blessing.",
