   "content": "<p>Verse no. 272</p><p>لَيْسَ عَلَيْكَ هُدٰىهُمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَهْدِيْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلِاَنْفُسِكُمْ ؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْنَ اِلَّا ابْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يُّوَفَّ اِلَيْكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تُظْلَمُوْنَ</p><p>Translation: (O Prophet ﷺ) you are not responsible for the guidance of these people; rather Allah grants guidance to whomever He wishes. And believers! whatever wealth you spend, its benefit is to you alone. And whatever you spend, you will spend for the pleasure of Allah. And whatever wealth you spend will be repaid to you in full, and no loss of any kind will be done to you.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed verse Allah the Exalted addresses Hazrat Muhammad ﷺ and says that the people who do not accept guidance, do not accept your ﷺ invitation as it should be accepted, and do not follow you ﷺ — then you ﷺ should not worry; guidance is not in their fate at all. You ﷺ will not be questioned about their not accepting guidance. Because of their deeds Allah has not guided them. Then it was said that whatever the people of faith spend out of their wealth, they will be repaid for it in full. Whatever they spend for the pleasure of Allah the Exalted, Allah the Exalted will give them even more than that, and no loss of any kind will be done to them.</p><p>Some people avoid spending in the way of God out of this fear, that perhaps in this way their wealth will decrease and they will become poor. Whereas by spending in the way of Allah wealth does not decrease; rather blessing arises in it. It becomes safe from every kind of danger and becomes the guarantor of the success of believers in both worlds. Through spending in the way of Allah too, Allah the Exalted tests the people of faith and raises the ranks of those who spend.</p>",
