   "content": "<p>Special study of selected ahadith</p><p>Hadith no. 26</p><p>عَنْ بَهْزِ بْنِ حَكِيْمٍ عَنْ اَبِيْهِ عَنْ جَدِّهٖ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ قَالَ سَمِعْتُ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُوْلُ: وَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْ يُحَدِّثُ بِالْحَدِيْثِ لِيُضْحِكَ بِهِ الْقَوْمَ فَيَكْذِبُ وَيْلٌ لَّهٗ وَيْلٌ لَّهٗ (سنن الترمذی)</p><p>Translation: Bahz bin Hakim narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he ﷺ was saying: Ruin is for that person who tells lies to make his people laugh. Ruin is for him, ruin is for him.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed hadith the Noble Prophet ﷺ has given a warning to those people who tell lies in gatherings of their relatives and friends etc. to win applause. Islam has cursed the liar. The sense of another blessed saying of the Noble Prophet ﷺ is that in a believer there can be evil of every kind, but he cannot be a liar. In the same way, telling the signs of the hypocrites, the saying of the Noble Prophet ﷺ is that one of his signs is also this, that when he speaks he tells a lie.</p><p>It has generally been seen that people tell lies to become the life of the gathering, and often merely for amusement. They take the support of false information, and merely to please others for the moment they make up things from their own side …</p>",
