   "content": "<p>… make. A severe warning has been given for such people that ruin is for them. By ruin is meant that they will remain in loss in this world too, and success in the Hereafter too will not come to their share.</p><p>Therefore we should always hold fast to truth, and never tell a lie, nor ever adopt this low habit for amusement. We should always keep this matter in mind, that we are the followers of the Prophet &quot;as-Sadiq&quot; (the Truthful). We should make truthfulness our way of life.</p><p>Hadith no. 27</p><p>عَنْ مَكْحُوْلٍ رَحِمَهُ اللّٰهُ اَنَّ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: اَلْعِلْمُ بِالتَّعَلُّمِ وَالْخَيْرُ عَادَةٌ وَاِذَا اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ خَيْرًا فَقَّهَهٗ فِي الدِّيْنِ (الجامع فی الحدیث: 446، مولفہ عبداللہ بن وہب المصری)</p><p>Translation: Knowledge comes by learning, and goodness is a nature (habit). And when Allah the Exalted intends good for someone, He grants him understanding of the religion.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed hadith he ﷺ said that the promotion, spread and progress of knowledge happens only when it is taught to others. Those societies and nations make the most progress where the process of teaching and instruction continues. In this pure hadith goodness has been declared a habit. Its meaning is that goodness becomes firm in a person&#x27;s behaviour only when it becomes his habit — that is, in daily affairs and routines he goes on doing good deeds involuntarily. And in this way a time comes when his morals become excellent.</p><p>In this blessed hadith it has also been said that when Allah intends good for someone, He grants him understanding of the religion. As it were, the understanding of the religion of Islam is a very great reward from Allah the Exalted. Fortunate are those individuals whom Allah the Exalted …</p>",
