   "content": "<p>… will remove the fire. Stopping backbiting is obligatory, firstly because helping one another is obligatory on every Muslim. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: &quot;A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim; he neither wrongs him nor abandons helping him.&quot; (Bukhari)</p><p>Secondly, because forbidding evil is obligatory on every Muslim according to his capacity. The Noble Messenger ﷺ said: &quot;Whoever among you sees an evil, let him stop it with his hand; if he does not have this strength, then with his tongue; if he does not have even this strength, then with his heart — and this is the weakest degree of faith.&quot; (Muslim)</p><p>(2) If one cannot stop the backbiting, what should one do: In a gathering where the commands of Allah the Exalted are being violated and they are being mocked, then the person sitting in that gathering too will be like them. The saying of the Exalted Creator is: &quot;And indeed Allah has sent down this command upon you in the Book, that when you hear that the verses of Allah are being denied and mocked, then as long as those people do not engage in other talk, do not sit near them, otherwise you too will be counted like them. There is no doubt that Allah is going to gather the hypocrites and the disbelievers in Hell.&quot; (An-Nisa: 140)</p><p>Hadith no. 30</p><p>عَنْ عُقْبَةَ بْنِ عَامِرٍ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ لَقِيْتُ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ يَوْمًا فَقُلْتُ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ مَا النَّجَاةُ؟ فَقَالَ: يَا عُقْبَةُ اَمْلِكْ عَلَيْكَ لِسَانَكَ وَلْيَسَعْكَ بَيْتُكَ وَابْكِ عَلٰى خَطِيْئَتِكَ (سنن الترمذی کتاب الذھد: حدیث نمبر ۲۴۰۶)</p><p>Translation: It is narrated from Uqbah bin Amir that one day I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him what salvation is. He ﷺ said: O Uqbah, keep your tongue under control, stay in your house, and weep over your faults.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed hadith the practical wisdom regarding attaining salvation has been told. For attaining salvation and safety …</p>",
