   "content": "<p>… three things have been prescribed.</p><p>1. Keeping the tongue under control</p><p>2. Staying at home (reforming the household)</p><p>3. Weeping over sins.</p><p>In daily routines countless quarrels and disorders arise only from wrong words that come out of the tongue. That is why it comes in a hadith that there is safety in silence; that is, one should say a good thing, otherwise one should remain silent. The principle &quot;first think, then speak&quot; is called better for this very reason, so that no such thing comes out of the mouth from which unpleasantness of any kind may arise.</p><p>By staying at home, or running towards home, is meant that from unnecessary wandering many evils are born. Staying at home and spending time with the household, being of use to them, and moreover giving them good upbringing, is a matter of good fortune. At the end it has been said that a person commits many sins knowingly or unknowingly. By shedding tears of remorse over them, seeking forgiveness, and repenting in the court of Allah the Exalted, a person will obtain salvation, and in this way he will also refrain from committing further sins.</p><p>Hadith no. 31</p><p>عَنْ اَبِيْ هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ اَنَّهٗ قِيْلَ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ مَا الْغِيْبَةُ؟ قَالَ: ذِكْرُكَ اَخَاكَ بِمَا يَكْرَهُ قِيْلَ اَفَرَاَيْتَ اِنْ كَانَ فِيْ اَخِيْ مَا اَقُوْلُ؟ قَالَ اِنْ كَانَ فِيْهِ مَا تَقُوْلُ فَقَدِ اغْتَبْتَهٗ وَاِنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ فِيْهِ مَا تَقُوْلُ فَقَدْ بَهَتَّهٗ (سنن ابی داؤد کتاب الادب باب فی الغیبۃ۔ حدیث ۴۸۷۴)</p><p>Translation: Hazrat Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with them) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what backbiting is. He ﷺ said: to mention such a thing of your brother which he dislikes. Then he asked: if that thing which I say is present in him? He ﷺ said: if what you say is present in him, then you backbit him; and if it is not present in him, then you slandered him.</p>",
