   "content": "<p>Explanation</p><p>Probably this matter had been revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or for some reason he had a doubt about him, that this man&#x27;s parents were in need of his service and he had come for jihad leaving them without their permission; therefore he ﷺ gave him this command, that he go back home and serve his parents, because in such a state the service of parents comes first for him. Drawing this conclusion from this hadith would be wrong, that whoever has parents should never go out of the house for jihad and for some service of the religion, and that only those people should engage in jihad and in the service of the religion whose parents are not alive. Among the noble Companions who used to do jihad with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a large number were of those whose parents were alive.</p><p>Hadith no. 35</p><p>عَنْ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمَا اَنَّ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: اَلْمُسْلِمُ اَخُو الْمُسْلِمِ لَا يَظْلِمُهٗ، وَلَا يُسْلِمُهٗ، وَمَنْ كَانَ فِيْ حَاجَةِ اَخِيْهِ كَانَ اللّٰهُ فِيْ حَاجَتِهٖ، وَمَنْ فَرَّجَ عَنْ مُسْلِمٍ كُرْبَةً فَرَّجَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ كُرْبَةً مِّنْ كُرُبَاتِ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَمَنْ سَتَرَ مُسْلِمًا سَتَرَهُ اللّٰهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ (صحیح البخاری کتاب المظالم حدیث نمبر ۲۴۴۲)</p><p>Translation: It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: a Muslim is the brother of another Muslim; he neither wrongs him nor abandons him in any calamity. And whoever remains engaged in fulfilling the need of his brother, Allah the Exalted keeps fulfilling his needs; and whoever removes the hardship of some Muslim, Allah the Exalted will remove from him a hardship among the hardships of the Day of Judgement; and whoever covers (the faults of) some Muslim, Allah the Exalted will cover him on the Day of Judgement.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed hadith it is stated that Muslims are brothers among themselves. The bond of religion is (above) all …</p>",
