   "content": "<p>… is a strong bond. The demand of this bond is that if ever a difference arises between two Muslim brothers or groups, they should make peace among themselves according to the command of Allah the Exalted and His Messenger ﷺ, fear Allah, and not be the least slack in it, so that the difference does not grow and Muslims do not shed one another&#x27;s blood. Along with this, in this noble hadith encouragement has also been given to this, that one Muslim should himself avoid ever wronging another Muslim, and should stop others too from wronging any Muslim, and should not hand over any Muslim to an oppressive government or person; rather he should help that Muslim in every possible way, as encouragement has been given in this noble hadith that whoever helps his brother in his work, Allah the Exalted will help him in his work; and whoever removes the calamity of his Muslim brother in this world, Allah the Exalted in return for it will remove his calamity on the Day of Judgement. In the same way a Muslim should overlook the faults of another Muslim; if he does not tell others or the disbelievers his faults and shortcomings, then Allah the Exalted too, on the hardest day of Judgement, will cast a veil over his faults, just as he had cast a veil over the faults of his Muslim brother in the world.</p><p>Hadith no. 36</p><p>عَنْ اَبِيْ هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ اَنَّهٗ قَالَ: اَلْمُؤْمِنُ مِرْاٰةُ الْمُؤْمِنِ وَالْمُؤْمِنُ اَخُو الْمُؤْمِنِ يَكُفُّ عَلَيْهِ ضَيْعَتَهٗ وَيَحُوْطُهٗ مِنْ وَّرَآئِهٖ (سنن ابی داؤد: 4918)</p><p>Translation: Hazrat Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) himself transmits the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he says: a believer is a mirror for another believer, and a believer is the brother of another believer; he protects his property and estate and protects him in his absence.</p>",
