   "content": "<p>Explanation</p><p>In this hadith the excellence of the merchant who deals gently with one in hardship is mentioned. In the economic system of Islam such teachings have been given which are no less than glad tidings for the needy, the destitute, widows, orphans and helpless people. Helping the poverty-stricken through qard-e-hasanah (benevolent loans), sadaqah and khayrat, zakat, and the teachings of forgiving loans — these Islamic teachings are such principles, by acting upon which poverty can be ended from society, and deprived classes can get the opportunity to stand on their own feet.</p><p>The Noble Prophet ﷺ has given heart-refreshing glad tidings to such a merchant who, seeing some poverty-stricken person in hardship, or while dealing with him, tells his companion to forgive him, that is, give him something free of charge; and if he is a debtor, then forgive his loan; it is possible that by the alms of this deed Allah the Exalted forgives us too. Allah the Exalted becomes pleased with such a person who deals gently with some poor and destitute servant of His.</p><p>We should show special sympathy with the poor in mutual dealings, and create ease for them, so that Allah the Exalted becomes pleased with us and forgives us.</p><p>Hadith no. 40</p><p>عَنِ النُّعْمَانِ بْنِ بَشِيْرٍ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُوْلُ: اَلْحَلَالُ بَيِّنٌ وَّالْحَرَامُ بَيِّنٌ وَّبَيْنَهُمَا مُشَبَّهَاتٌ لَا يَعْلَمُهَا كَثِيْرٌ مِّنَ النَّاسِ، فَمَنِ اتَّقَى الْمُشَبَّهَاتِ اسْتَبْرَاَ لِدِيْنِهٖ وَعِرْضِهٖ وَمَنْ وَّقَعَ فِي الشُّبُهَاتِ وَقَعَ فِي الْحَرَامِ كَرَاعٍ يَّرْعٰى حَوْلَ الْحِمٰى يُوْشِكُ اَنْ يُّوَاقِعَهٗ: اَلَا وَاِنَّ لِكُلِّ مَلِكٍ حِمًى، اَلَا اِنَّ حِمَى اللّٰهِ مَحَارِمُهٗ، اَلَا وَاِنَّ فِي الْجَسَدِ مُضْغَةً اِذَا صَلَحَتْ صَلَحَ الْجَسَدُ كُلُّهٗ وَاِذَا فَسَدَتْ فَسَدَ الْجَسَدُ كُلُّهٗ، اَلَا وَهِيَ الْقَلْبُ (صحیح البخاری کتاب الایمان حدیث نمبر ۵۲)</p>",
