   "content": "<p>Hadith no. 42</p><p>عَنْ اَبِيْ اَيُّوْبَ الْاَنْصَارِيِّ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ اَنَّ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: &quot;لَا يَحِلُّ لِرَجُلٍ اَنْ يَّهْجُرَ اَخَاهُ فَوْقَ ثَلٰثِ لَيَالٍ يَلْتَقِيَانِ، فَيُعْرِضُ هٰذَا، وَيُعْرِضُ هٰذَا۔ وَخَيْرُهُمَا الَّذِيْ يَبْدَاُ بِالسَّلَامِ&quot; (صحیح مسلم و صحیح البخاری)</p><p>Translation: Hazrat Abu Ayyub al-Ansari narrates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: &quot;It is not lawful for any man that he abandon his brother for more than three days. When they meet each other, one turns his face this way and the other that way; and the better of the two is the one who takes the initiative in greeting.&quot;</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed hadith a limit has been fixed in the case of displeasure between Muslims, that if ever over a mutual fight, quarrel or some matter displeasure arises, then cutting off relations is permissible for at most three days. After that, two Muslim brothers remaining displeased has been declared unlawful.</p><p>In this blessed hadith urging has been made for the promotion of mutual love, and this advice has been given that, living together, often grievance arises among them and a person begins to turn away from another. It was said that this turning away should not be longer than three days, otherwise it will be a grave sin. Although, for ending the displeasure between two Muslim brothers, a third should step forward and get the displeasure ended, so that the two Muslims again become like milk and sugar. If this is not possible, then any one of them should take courage and take the initiative, and at meeting should greet first. In Islam, the one who first ends the displeasure has been declared better. One who ends false ego and stubbornness is truly great. That is why his ﷺ blessed saying is that the strong man is not the one who throws another down in a contest, but rather the strong man is the one who controls his anger.</p>",
