   "content": "<p>Hadith no. 43</p><p>عَنْ اَبِيْ هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ، قَالَ: مَا عَابَ النَّبِيُّ (صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ) طَعَامًا قَطُّ، اِنِ اشْتَهَاهُ اَكَلَهٗ وَاِلَّا تَرَكَهٗ (صحیح مسلم و صحیح البخاری)</p><p>Translation: It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet ﷺ never found fault with food; if he liked it he would eat it, otherwise he would leave it.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed hadith teaching has been given about things to eat and drink. Hazrat Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet of the Last Age, Hazrat Muhammad Mustafa ﷺ, never in his life found defect in things to eat and drink. The thing which he liked, he ﷺ would partake of, and if he did not like that thing, he simply would not eat it.</p><p>Eating and drinking is a basic need of man. We eat many things every day. It has often been seen that finding fault in things to eat, and searching for defect, has become our habit. All the things to eat and drink are blessings of Allah the Exalted. We should, eating the blessings of Allah, give thanks for them, and if some thing is not liked, or the taste of some thing does not seem good, then withdraw the hand and become silent. Finding fault in things to eat is on one side disobedience to Allah the Exalted, and on the other side it is also a cause of hurting the hearts of those who present that thing. We, acting upon the beautiful example of our beloved Messenger Hazrat Muhammad ﷺ, should never find defect in things to eat.</p>",
