   "content": "<p>Explanation</p><p>In this blessed hadith the Noble Prophet ﷺ has given his Ummah a universal message: that no Muslim, holding some weapon in his hand, should point it towards some Muslim brother of his, lest Satan, by his hands, cause harm to another with the weapon. He ﷺ said this at a time when sword, spear, bow and arrow etc. were (the weapons). In the knowledge of the eye of prophethood it was that the coming time would be of the most modern weapons. Therefore it is quite possible that by pointing a weapon towards another, harm reaches him.</p><p>It has happened again and again that there was a gun in someone&#x27;s hand. By way of mischief, joking or by mistake he pointed it towards another and it went off. In this way the other person was killed unjustly, and the one who pointed the weapon towards the other was left wringing his hands in regret forever.</p><p>In the present age the importance of this hadith has increased manifold, because the most modern weapons have been made which can go off with a little carelessness or lack of caution. Therefore we should, if there is a weapon of any kind in our hand, not point it towards others.</p><p>Hadith no. 47</p><p>عَنْ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمَا اَنَّ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: عُذِّبَتِ امْرَاَةٌ فِيْ هِرَّةٍ سَجَنَتْهَا حَتّٰى مَاتَتْ، فَدَخَلَتْ فِيْهَا النَّارَ، لَا هِيَ اَطْعَمَتْهَا، وَلَا سَقَتْهَا اِذْ حَبَسَتْهَا وَلَا هِيَ تَرَكَتْهَا تَاْكُلُ مِنْ خَشَاشِ الْاَرْضِ (صحیح مسلم و صحیح البخاری)</p><p>Translation: It is narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: a woman was punished because of a cat which was in her captivity until it died. So because of this that woman was thrown into Hell. She neither fed it nor gave it water when she had kept it captive, nor let it go so that it could eat the insects of the earth.</p>",
