   "content": "<p>Hadith no. 49</p><p>عَنْ اَبِيْ هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ: &quot;يَقُوْلُ اللّٰهُ تَعَالٰى اَنَا عِنْدَ ظَنِّ عَبْدِيْ بِيْ، وَاَنَا مَعَهٗ اِذَا ذَكَرَنِيْ، فَاِنْ ذَكَرَنِيْ فِيْ نَفْسِهٖ، ذَكَرْتُهٗ فِيْ نَفْسِيْ، وَاِنْ ذَكَرَنِيْ فِيْ مَلَاٍ، ذَكَرْتُهٗ فِيْ مَلَاٍ خَيْرٍ مِّنْهُمْ، وَاِنْ تَقَرَّبَ اِلَيَّ بِشِبْرٍ تَقَرَّبْتُ اِلَيْهِ ذِرَاعًا، وَاِنْ تَقَرَّبَ اِلَيَّ ذِرَاعًا، تَقَرَّبْتُ اِلَيْهِ بَاعًا، وَاِنْ اَتَانِيْ يَمْشِيْ، اَتَيْتُهٗ هَرْوَلَةً&quot; (صحیح مسلم و صحیح البخاری)</p><p>Translation: Hazrat Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet ﷺ said: Allah the Exalted says: I am according to My servant&#x27;s opinion of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. When he remembers Me in his heart, I remember him in My heart; and when he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better than that. When he comes one span towards Me, I come one cubit towards him; and if he comes one cubit, I come two arms&#x27; length; and when he comes walking, I come running towards him.</p><p>Explanation</p><p>This blessed hadith is a hadith qudsi. A hadith qudsi is that in which the Noble Prophet ﷺ says that Allah the Exalted says that …</p><p>In this blessed hadith the special favours of divine mercy are mentioned. Allah the Exalted loves His servants immensely. In some ahadith it comes that Allah loves His servants even more than seventy mothers. In Surah al-Baqarah it has been said that when some servant calls upon Allah, Allah answers his call.</p>",
