   "content": "<p>Muslim experts of economics</p><p>Like the other sciences, Muslims compiled an excellent treasure of knowledge and wisdom in the science of economics too, in the form of books and laws, which obtained legal status and was also made prevalent in practical form. Among Muslim experts of economics the following obtained the greatest fame.</p><p>1. Imam Abu Yusuf (may Allah have mercy on him)</p><p>2. Abu &#x27;Ubayd al-Qasim bin Sallam (may Allah have mercy on him)</p><p>3. Allama Ibn Hazm (may Allah have mercy on him)</p><p>4. Allama Ibn Khaldun (may Allah have mercy on him) and</p><p>5. Shah Waliullah (may Allah have mercy on him) are worth mentioning.</p><p>Imam Abu Yusuf (may Allah have mercy on him) wrote many books, among which, with respect to economic thought, &quot;Kitab al-Kharaj&quot; holds great importance. In it he gave principles regarding the collection of kharaj from crops obtained from lands, and declared partnership better than kharaj. Besides this, in his book Amali the principles of the collection of revenues have been discussed.</p><p>Abu &#x27;Ubayd al-Qasim bin Sallam (may Allah have mercy on him) too wrote many books, among which some obtained lasting fame. He wrote &quot;Kitab al-Amwal&quot; about the financial system. He for the first time made clear the method of collecting &#x27;ushur in the Islamic state, that in a year &#x27;ushur should be taken from a trader only once, however many times he may pass by the one collecting &#x27;ushur. Besides this he wrote books on jizyah, kharaj, iqta&#x27;, ghanimah and the difference of fay&#x27;, and hima (pasture) and collective interest.</p><p>Allama Ibn Hazm was a thinker, expert of economics and scholar. In the economic system of Islam his services cannot fail to be acknowledged. The living and eternal achievement of his economic thought exists in the form of his work &quot;al-Muhalla&quot;, which he wrote in an extremely easy-to-understand and comprehensive style.</p><p>The name of Allama Ibn Khaldun holds special importance among experts of economics and thinkers. Robert Flint says that:</p>",
