   "content": "<p>One issue in the Ummah is also this, that some people engage in the knowledge of religion in such a way that they do not even tolerate looking towards worldly sciences, whereas those who study worldly sciences generally become estranged from religion, because of which Muslim society has been divided into two classes and each class considers the other its rival. This attitude becomes the cause of widening the gulf of division; therefore this division of the modern-educated and the mulla should be ended, and every class should create the means of benefiting from the other class, so that the sciences of both kinds become helpers of one another and walk on the path of progress, so that the conspiracies of others may be uprooted and the advanced imperialist powers may be properly confronted, which want to weaken Muslims in both religious and worldly fields and establish their dominance over them, and want to take possession of all mineral resources and atomic resources.</p><p>In the present era, knowledge has progressed greatly in the fields of science and technology. But the regret is that people are using it in wrong works too. In spreading knowledge this matter is necessary, that every individual use it in a positive manner for the welfare and well-being of people, through which the country and nation may progress. When every human being adopts this attitude and thinking, then certainly the future of the Muslim Ummah will be bright.</p><p>While acquiring and spreading knowledge, prejudice should not be given a place. Every individual should consider himself an individual of the Ummah, not an individual of some particular region or group. Likewise this is most necessary, that wherever we can help someone else in acquiring knowledge, there we should play our role. In the spread of knowledge and the acquisition of knowledge we should help others fully.</p><p>Exercise</p><p>Question 1: Write the answers to the following questions.</p><p>i. Throw light on the services of Muslims with reference to religious sciences.</p><p>ii. What are the Sihah Sittah called? State their details.</p><p>iii. State the features of the Islamic economic system.</p><p>iv. What feats did Muslims accomplish in scientific sciences?</p>",
