   "content": "<p>v. Which elements make man sociable?</p><p>vi. In your opinion, in which branch did Muslims work the most?</p><p>vii. How can Muslims attain academic ascendancy in the present age?</p><p>viii. What outstanding feats did Muslims accomplish in Andalus?</p><p>ix. What were the causes of the academic neglect of Muslims?</p><p>Question 2: Put a (✓) mark on the most suitable answer according to the lesson.</p><p> i. With reference to knowledge, the first verses were revealed</p><p>(a) in Surah al-Fatihah  (b) in Surah al-Kawthar</p><p>(c) in Surah al-&#x27;Alaq  (d) in Surah al-Baqarah</p><p> ii. Which country is famous for the academic progress of Muslims?</p><p>(a) Saudi Arabia  (b) Pakistan</p><p>(c) Andalus  (d) Turkey</p><p> iii. For whom is the knowledge of nasikh and mansukh extremely necessary?</p><p>(a) principles of tafsir  (b) principles of hadith</p><p>(c) principles of fiqh  (d) tasawwuf</p><p> iv. The Muslim mathematician was</p><p>(a) al-Khwarizmi  (b) Jabir bin Hayyan</p><p>(c) Tariq bin Ziyad  (d) Muhammad bin Qasim</p><p>Question 3: Give short answers to the following questions.</p><p>i. State the definition of usul al-fiqh.</p><p>ii. What is meant by just distribution in the Islamic economic system?</p><p>iii. Throw light on enjoining good and forbidding evil in Islam.</p><p>Activity</p><p>The teacher should hold a written competition among the students whose title is &quot;Causes and effects of academic neglect in the era of decline&quot;.</p>",
