   "content": "<p>… and when the time came that spark became a flame. However, along with freedom some such elements crept in which were strangers to the spirit of the Islamic ideology of life. This is the reason that even in the Muslim country the demand for an Islamic state gained strength, although Muslim countries should naturally be Islamic states, and all their energies should be spent only for the promotion of the Islamic state. But unfortunately we do not see such a situation. Its big reasons are as follows.</p><p>a. The majority being devoid of real Islamic teachings.</p><p>b. The rulers in power being overawed by Western powers.</p><p>c. The modern-educated class being distant from Islamic teachings.</p><p>d. Muslims remaining entangled in subsidiary differences.</p><p>e. The forces of ijtihad going into the background.</p><p>f. The prejudices created by the West gaining promotion.</p><p>g. Being backward scientifically, in research and academically.</p><p>h. Westernised systems of education remaining current.</p><p>i. Considering real Islamic teachings outdated.</p><p>j. Mutual unity and harmony and cooperation becoming extinct.</p><p>These are the elements which are the biggest obstacle in the establishment of the Islamic state. The best method of removing these obstacles can only be this, that real Islamic teachings be spread on a wide scale, and such education and training of the new generation be done that they become free mentally, in heart and spiritually. They should be reminded of the forgotten lessons of faith, trust in Allah, contentment, continuous action, and the conquest of the universe, so that, respecting the sentiments and feelings of the great majority of Muslims, they come out into the field of action, and, using their God-given abilities in a positive manner, bring forth within themselves such leadership which becomes the guarantor of the establishment of the Islamic state.</p><p>With the passage of time, in most Muslim countries such movements are being born which are compelling rulers to think about the establishment of the Islamic state. Among these countries Turkey, Malaysia, Bangladesh, Iran, Egypt, Syria, Iraq, Pakistan and the Middle …</p>",
