   "theory": "The efforts for establishing an Islamic state bearing the above qualities can be divided into the following branches.\n\na. Educational efforts\n\nb. Efforts of ijtihad\n\nc. Economic efforts\n\nd. Social efforts\n\ne. Judicial efforts\n\nf. Scientific efforts\n\nNewly arising issues should be solved through ijtihad. No individual of the Muslim Ummah should remain ignorant and uneducated. Economic and social unevenness should end. The nation should progress scientifically and in research. Law-making should take place in the light of the Quran and Hadith, and the executive should get it acted upon honestly; and if anywhere there is violation of the law, then justice should be seen being done in the courts.\n\nHow positive Islamic change can be brought about in this country — for achieving this purpose the following proposals are presented.\n\nRenewal of faith\n\nFor this great work Muslims need to prepare themselves and bring change within themselves. For this the first preparation is that Muslims bring a new and fresh faith in Islam. There is absolutely no need of a new religion, a new prophet, a new Shari'ah and a new teaching for Islam. Islam, like the sun, was never old, nor is it old now. The prophethood of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is the permanent and last prophethood. His ﷺ religion is preserved and his ﷺ teachings are alive, but new mischiefs, new powers, new temptations and new invitations cannot be confronted with weak faith and wounded customs and habits. Muslims will have to conquer the present materialism and doubt and anxiety, and create within themselves a new spirit of faith, fresh certainty and fresh zeal.",
