   "content": "<p>Surah al-Duha</p><p>Introduction</p><p>This surah is Makki, and the Makki era is the era of severe trial in the life of him ﷺ. In the context of these circumstances Allah the Exalted sent down this surah. Allah the Exalted described the station and rank of His beloved, and the best of creation, Hazrat Muhammad ﷺ, and mentioned the worldly and other-worldly rewards and favours which were to be upon him ﷺ after the hardships of this Makki era.</p><p>At the beginning Allah the Exalted has sworn an oath. Then the rewards of the Hereafter are mentioned. Then the circumstances of his ﷺ childhood are recalled, that he ﷺ was brought up in the state of orphanhood; and at the end He completed the surah with three instructions: that he ﷺ show compassion to orphans, have mercy on the needy, and wipe the tears of the destitute.</p><p>اَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ الرَّجِيْمِ</p><p>بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ</p><p>وَالضُّحٰى ۞ وَالَّيْلِ اِذَا سَجٰى ۞ مَا وَدَّعَكَ رَبُّكَ وَمَا قَلٰى ۞ وَلَلْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لَّكَ مِنَ الْاُوْلٰى ۞ وَلَسَوْفَ يُعْطِيْكَ رَبُّكَ فَتَرْضٰى ۞ اَلَمْ يَجِدْكَ يَتِيْمًا فَاٰوٰى ۞ وَوَجَدَكَ ضَآلًّا فَهَدٰى ۞ وَوَجَدَكَ عَآئِلًا فَاَغْنٰى ۞ فَاَمَّا الْيَتِيْمَ فَلَا تَقْهَرْ ۞ وَاَمَّا السَّآئِلَ فَلَا تَنْهَرْ ۞ وَاَمَّا بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ فَحَدِّثْ</p><p>Translation: By the brightness of the sun, and by the darkness of the night when it covers. O Prophet ﷺ, your Lord has neither left you nor is He displeased with you. And the Hereafter is far better for you than the world. And your Lord will soon grant you so much that you will be pleased. Did He not find you an orphan and give you shelter? …</p>",
