   "content": "<p>[gharartu] I deceived.</p><p>[kaffah] All.</p><p>[latubʿathunna] You will certainly be raised again after death.</p><p>[latamutunna] Death will certainly come to you.</p><p>[latuhasabunna] Your account will certainly be taken.</p><p>[latujzawunna] You will certainly be given recompense.</p><p>[abadan] Forever.</p><p>Commentary: In this sermon Huzoor ﷺ made his family aware about the Hereafter. We see these features in this sermon.</p><p>1. Brevity</p><p>2. Easy words</p><p>3. Simile: death has been likened to sleep and coming alive again to waking.</p><p>4. Style of emphasis: to stress his point he ﷺ adopted the style of emphasis — you will certainly die, etc.</p><p>He ﷺ established the custom of praise and glorification at the beginning of the sermon.</p><p>The Farewell Sermon</p><p>يٰٓاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنَّهٗ لَا نَبِيَّ بَعْدِيْ وَلَآ اُمَّةَ بَعْدَكُمْ ۞ اَلَا فَاعْبُدُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ۞ وَصَلُّوْا خَمْسَكُمْ ۞ وَصُوْمُوْا شَهْرَكُمْ وَاَدُّوْا زَكٰوةَ اَمْوَالِكُمْ طَيِّبَةً بِهَا اَنْفُسُكُمْ ۞ وَتَحُجُّوْنَ بَيْتَ رَبِّكُمْ ۞ وَاَطِيْعُوْا وُلَاةَ اَمْرِكُمْ ۞ تَدْخُلُوْا جَنَّةَ رَبِّكُمْ</p><p>Translation: O people! There is no prophet after me, nor will any Ummah be born after you. Beware! So worship your Lord, and offer your five daily prayers, and keep the fasts of your month (Ramadan), and pay the zakat of your wealth with willing hearts, and perform the Hajj of the House of your Lord, and obey your rulers; you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.</p><p>(Ibn Jarir, Ibn &#x27;Asakir from Abu Umamah)</p><p>Difficult words and meanings:</p><p>[la nabiyya ba&#x27;di] There will be no prophet after me.</p><p>[tadkhulu] You will enter.</p><p>[wulat] Plural of wali (rulers).</p><p>[addu] Pay.</p><p>[ala] Beware.</p><p>[bayt] House.</p>",
