     "text": "… and sajdah by gesture, let him pray. This is better than praying standing with ruku' and sajdah. And making the intention without a pause, that is, a connected intention; and the condition is that he knows well which prayer he is offering. And for nafl, Sunnah and tarawih an unqualified intention is sufficient. And for the obligatory prayer, specifying it too is necessary — for example (he is offering) the 'Asr prayer. And the follower should also intend praying behind the imam; and in the funeral prayer he should intend the prayer for Allah and supplication for the deceased. And facing towards the qiblah: so for one living in Makkah, facing towards the Ka'bah itself is obligatory, and for those outside, facing only the direction of the qiblah is obligatory. And one who prays the prayer of fear may pray in whatever direction he is able; and one who has doubt about the direction of the qiblah should investigate (in which direction the qiblah is); and if the direction is proved wrong, he need not repeat the prayer; and if it becomes known during the prayer, he should turn towards that direction.",
