   "content": "<p>… created from a handful of clay gathered from the whole earth. So the children of Adam (peace be upon him) came in accordance with the earth: among them some are red, some white, some black, and some in between; and among them some are hard-tempered and some soft-tempered, and some impure and some pure.&quot; Then Hazrat Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: what thing makes the child resemble its father or mother? So he ﷺ said: when the fluid of the man takes precedence over the fluid of the woman, then its resemblance is with the boy, and when the fluid of the woman takes precedence over the fluid of the man, then its resemblance is with the girl. And I know of no one who doubts this, that the cause of death is the blow of a sword or eating poison, and that the creation of the child in the mother&#x27;s womb takes place after the falling of semen, and the creation of seeds and trees takes place after sowing seed, planting and watering. And for this capacity responsibility has come, and they have been given commands, and they have been forbidden, and they have been given recompense for their deeds. So among these powers (upon which the acts of Allah are ordered) are the properties and temperaments of the elements; and among them are the commands which Allah has placed in the form of every kind; among them are the conditions of the world of images and of existence, about which a decision was made there before existence on the earth; and among them are the supplications of the higher assembly (al-mala&#x27; al-a&#x27;la), which are made with their full effort for those who refined their souls (that is, purified the self) or strove for the reform of people.</p><p>Lexical explanation:</p><p>[al-naql] By it are meant the heavenly sciences, like the Quran and Hadith etc.</p><p>[al-&#x27;aql] By it are meant the worldly sciences.</p><p>[qubdah] A handful.</p><p>[yanzi&#x27;] To resemble, to draw.</p><p>[&#x27;aqib] After.</p><p>[al-hubub] Grains, seeds.</p><p>[al-badhr] To sow seed.</p><p>[al-ghars] To plant a sapling.</p><p>[al-saqy] To give water.</p><p>Commentary:</p><p>In this extract Hazrat Shah Waliullah (may Allah have mercy on him) has discussed this topic, that the practice of Allah does not change. The birth of a child takes place only from the union of man and woman. A tree and plant is born only after the sowing of seed.</p>",
