   "content": "<p>Lexical explanation:</p><p>[mawliduhu] Birthplace.</p><p>[ta&#x27;abbada] Became devoted to worship.</p><p>[muqni&#x27;an] Covered.</p><p>[awma&#x27;tu] I pointed.</p><p>[taqalladta] You took responsibility.</p><p>[badrah] A purse of ten thousand dirhams.</p><p>[dha dayn] Debtor.</p><p>[fa-ista&#x27;fa] Excused himself.</p><p>[tabat] To be lawful.</p><p>Commentary</p><p>Muruj al-Dhahab was written by al-Mas&#x27;udi on history. This extract is about Hazrat Fudayl &#x27;Iyad (may Allah have mercy on him), who was a man of Allah. The people of taqwa adopt indifference towards the world and wealth. This extract is written in the style of a story. It is full of literary qualities; moreover its language is simple and easy to understand.</p><p>Futuh al-Buldan of al-Baladhuri</p><p>This book was written by al-Baladhuri. His name is Ahmad bin Yahya bin Jabir bin Dawud al-Baladhuri (may Allah have mercy on him). He was born in Baghdad in the third century Hijri.</p><p>حَدَّثَنِيْ عَمْرُو بْنُ مُحَمَّدٍ النَّاقِدُ وَاَحْمَدُ بْنُ هِشَامِ بْنِ بَهْرَامَ قَالَا: حَدَّثَنَا وَكِيْعُ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ قَالَ: اَخْبَرَنَا رَبِيْعَةُ بْنُ عُثْمَانَ عَنْ عِمْرَانَ بْنِ اَبِيْ اَنَسٍ عَنْ سَهْلِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ قَالَ: اِخْتَلَفَ رَجُلَانِ عَلٰى عَهْدِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ الَّذِيْٓ اُسِّسَ عَلَى التَّقْوٰى، فَقَالَ اَحَدُهُمَا: هُوَ مَسْجِدُ الرَّسُوْلِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَالَ الْآخَرُ: هُوَ مَسْجِدُ قُبَا فَاَتَيَا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَآلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ فَسَاَلَاهُ فَقَالَ هُوَ مَسْجِدِيْ هٰذَا (صحیح ابن حبان (1604))</p>",
