   "content": "<p>Introduction of the authors</p><p>1. Ahmad Saeed</p><p>He passed M.A. Arabic and M.A. Islamiat with distinguished marks from the Islamia University Bahawalpur. He did M.Phil Arabic from the International Islamic University Islamabad. Under Allama Iqbal Open University Islamabad he kept training Arabic teachers for a period of ten years. Besides this, for the last 16 years he has been associated with the field of teaching. He has a deep attachment to authorship and compilation.</p><p>2. Dr Shafqat Ali Janjua</p><p>Dr Shafqat Ali Janjua belongs to the district of Kasur. He received education up to B.A. in Pattoki, district Kasur. After this he passed the B.Ed examination from Government Education College for Men, Lower Mall, Lahore. There his deep attachment to Urdu language and literature developed, and he achieved prominent success by adopting the teaching of Urdu and English subjects. He did M.A. in Islamic Studies from the Institute of Islamic Sciences, Punjab University Lahore, and then passed the M.Ed examination from the Institute of Education and Research, Punjab University. He began his practical life as a teacher at a model institution in Islamabad. He made a name in teaching Urdu at the secondary level, because of which he was declared the best teacher of the Urdu language. He was selected through the Federal Public Service Commission and served as an Education Officer in the Curriculum Wing of the Ministry of Education. He was also declared the &quot;best item writer&quot; in the Urdu language by the National Education Assessment System of the Ministry of Education. He has conducted many courses on the teaching of the Urdu language. During his posting in the Curriculum Wing, he prepared modules on various topics of population and education, which were highly praised and were approved for publication in the whole country. He is the author of four textbooks of Urdu too, and many articles written by him have been published in national newspapers. In 2005 he was selected through the Federal Public Service Commission as vice-principal for the institutions run under the Federal Directorate of Education Islamabad. Nowadays he is posted as vice-principal at Islamabad Model College for Boys G-6/2.</p><p>3. Niaz Muhammad</p><p>Niaz Muhammad is an active educationist. He belongs to Sarband, Peshawar. He obtained B.A. Honours from Shaykh Zayed Islamic Centre, and along with it degrees of M.A. Islamiat and M.A. Arabic from Peshawar University. For a long time he has been associated with the teaching of Islamiat and Arabic in a government …</p>",
